{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "label": "Mailbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exactly one per actor, and the thing that makes the one-message-at-a-time guarantee physically true."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_unboundeddefault", "label": "Unbounded FIFO default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The previous bounded default did not hold up: only the user queue was capped so the memory ceiling was not real, and a mailbox cannot tell what it is discarding \u2014 drop-head suits telemetry but not a Terminated signal or a WebSocket close. Loss is now something you ask for per actor, and growth is warned about at 10 000 messages and each doubling."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_boundedmailbox", "label": "BoundedMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Constructing one directly defaults to reject, because you built a bound and nothing else can be assumed about what is safe to lose; withMailboxOverflow defaults to drop-head, the policy suiting the workloads people reach for a bound to protect."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflowpolicy", "label": "Overflow policies (drop-head / drop-new / reject)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A backpressure-versus-loss trade-off: drop-head is freshest-wins for telemetry, drop-new is first-wins for command streams, reject is for a sender with a meaningful backoff response. reject throws at the tell site, so a full mailbox on B surfaces as A restarting."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_prioritymailbox", "label": "PriorityMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "priorityFor runs at enqueue time, lower numbers go first and ties break FIFO. Sorted-insertion is fine into the low thousands; a sustained backlog where insertion shows up in profiles is open to a heap-backed swap."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_prioritybounding", "label": "Bounding a priority mailbox", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "drop-head is deliberately not offered: on a priority queue the head is the message priorityFor called most important, so dropping it would defeat the reason for choosing this mailbox. prependUser re-runs the priority function, so a bounded priority mailbox can drop on unstash."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_systemmessageprecedence", "label": "System messages take absolute precedence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This is why supervision reacts instantly. ref.stop() does not jump the queue \u2014 it is a user message, so the actor drains what is already queued first."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_ringbuffer", "label": "RingBuffer-backed queues", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A queue with no ceiling has to stay cheap when deep: taking the next message advances an index instead of reindexing everything behind it, so delivering one message does not cost more as the backlog grows."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_dropreportingmailbox", "label": "DropReportingMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drop counting is labelled per actor class rather than per actor: shedding is what a bounded mailbox is for, so a per-actor label would mint a permanent series for every actor behaving as designed. Registration is additive, so a custom onDrop keeps firing beside the stock counter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailboxstash", "label": "Mailbox reinsertion on unstash", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The framework calls prependUser and the mailbox decides how to reinsert \u2014 a PriorityMailbox re-prioritizes and goes through the bound, BoundedMailbox bypasses it."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_actor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailboxstash", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_become_and_stash_stash", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_unboundeddefault", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_unboundeddefault", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_ringbuffer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_unboundeddefault", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflowpolicy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_boundedmailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_prioritymailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_boundedmailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflowpolicy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "s